(6075634, 892345, 83313, '<td valign="top">Feedback, per your request in the forums:<br/>I gave this a 4, I''m afraid. I didn''t feel the tilt added anything to the scene. Perhaps it was because the tree took up so much of the frame that the real subject was swallowed. I think if the view had been closer to the subject, it may have had more impact and the tilt would have lent a more dramatic feel to it. If I was shooting this scene, I think I would have tried to get on the ground, close to the guy catching the Frisbee, and used the wider end of my lens for a more dramatic perspective. I like those really strong perspectives, however.</td>', 'Feedback, per your request in the forums:I gave this a 4, I''m afraid. I didn''t feel the tilt added anything to the scene. Perhaps it was because the tree took up so much of the frame that the real subject was swallowed. I think if the view had been closer to the subject, it may have had more impact and the tilt would have lent a more dramatic feel to it. If I was shooting this scene, I think I would have tried to get on the ground, close to the guy catching the Frisbee, and used the wider end of my lens for a more dramatic perspective. I like those really strong perspectives, however.', '2010-07-01 10:30:40.000000', NULL, 0),
