(6088141, 892902, 68947, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the Top Ten Finish, Steve!  Way to go!!!  :)<br/> <br/>Having said that, I also need to say that while it''s a GREAT piece for DPC''s "Eye Candy Love", I do agree with you that your previous entry (shown in your notes above) DOES take the cake!  It''s pure and raw emotion and joy that you''ve captured!  I can FEEL her enthusiasm and child''s joy.  Unfortunately, that''s not what "sells" here in DPCland and that''s a shame.  I think you are evolving in recognizing the difference between what emotes something from a viewer and what''s considered "good photography" in DPC.  <br/> <br/>Congrats on BOTH shots as they both have their purposes and audiences. :)</td>', 'Congrats on the Top Ten Finish, Steve!  Way to go!!!  :) Having said that, I also need to say that while it''s a GREAT piece for DPC''s "Eye Candy Love", I do agree with you that your previous entry (shown in your notes above) DOES take the cake!  It''s pure and raw emotion and joy that you''ve captured!  I can FEEL her enthusiasm and child''s joy.  Unfortunately, that''s not what "sells" here in DPCland and that''s a shame.  I think you are evolving in recognizing the difference between what emotes something from a viewer and what''s considered "good photography" in DPC.   Congrats on BOTH shots as they both have their purposes and audiences. :)', '2010-07-11 13:03:31.000000', NULL, 0),
